---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';

const tiers = [
  {
    tier: 'Tier 1',
    name: 'Public',
    badge: 'Open / Context-Aware',
    icon: 'circle-check',
    desc: 'Callable without authentication or with optional caller identity context. Ideal for read-only queries, system capabilities, and public documentation searches.',
    features: [
      'Zero credential overhead for safe tools',
      'Optional caller identity injection',
      'Rate-limiting and telemetry ready',
    ],
  },
  {
    tier: 'Tier 2',
    name: 'Scoped Resource Guard',
    badge: 'OAuth 2.1 & RFC 9728',
    icon: 'shield-check',
    desc: 'Requires a valid bearer or RFC 9449 DPoP token verified via authkestra-resource. Missing or insufficient scopes trigger RFC 9728 resource metadata elicitation.',
    features: [
      'RFC 9728 /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource',
      'DPoP (RFC 9449) & mTLS (RFC 8705) sender binding',
      'Automatic 401 WWW-Authenticate challenge elicitation',
    ],
  },
  {
    tier: 'Tier 3',
    name: 'HumanApproved (HITL Step-Up)',
    badge: 'RFC 8785 JCS & Biometrics',
    icon: 'key',
    desc: 'Mandates cryptographic human approval bound to canonicalized tool parameters. Prevents unauthorized financial transfers, deletions, or external API execution.',
    features: [
      'RFC 8785 JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS)',
      'Deterministic SHA-256 challenge digest binding',
      'Physical WebAuthn Passkey / TOTP re-proof',
      'Atomic single-use token consumption (AtomicConsume)',
      'Deterministic parameter tampering rejection',
    ],
  },
];
---
<section id="ai-agents-mcp" class="ai-mcp" aria-labelledby="ai-mcp-heading">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="header">
      <div class="pill">
        <Icon name="bot" size={16} class="pill-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
        <span>authkestra-mcp</span>
      </div>
      <h2 id="ai-mcp-heading">AI Agent &amp; Model Context Protocol (MCP) Security</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Autonomous AI agents need access to tools, but giving LLMs unrestricted execution rights
        or raw API keys is an existential security risk. <code>authkestra-mcp</code> intercepts MCP
        JSON-RPC requests with three composable security tiers, cryptographic parameter binding,
        and zero-trust credential isolation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3-Tier Grid -->
    <div class="tiers-grid">
      {tiers.map((t) => (
        <div class="tier-card">
          <div class="tier-header">
            <span class="tier-num">{t.tier}</span>
            <span class="tier-badge">{t.badge}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tier-title-row">
            <div class="tier-icon-wrap">
              <Icon name={t.icon} size={20} class="tier-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
            </div>
            <h3>{t.name}</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="tier-desc">{t.desc}</p>
          <ul class="tier-features">
            {t.features.map((f) => (
              <li>
                <Icon name="check" size={14} class="feature-check" aria-hidden="true" />
                <span>{f}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <!-- Deep Dive Architecture: JCS Parameter Tamper & Token Vault -->
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-card">
        <div class="arch-icon-wrap">
          <Icon name="shield-alert" size={24} class="arch-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
        </div>
        <h3>Cryptographic JCS Parameter Tampering Defense</h3>
        <p>
          Prompt injections and model hallucinations can cause agents to alter critical arguments
          after receiving user approval. Authkestra solves this with strict <strong>RFC 8785 JSON
          Canonicalization Scheme (JCS)</strong>:
        </p>
        <div class="formula-box">
          <code>SHA-256(session_id ‖ tool_name ‖ JCS(args) ‖ expires_at)</code>
        </div>
        <p>
          If an adversary or model mutates even a single character, key ordering, or numeric value
          (e.g., <code>amount: 50</code> to <code>amount: 5000</code>) between approval and invocation,
          the challenge digest check fails instantly, aborting execution.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="arch-card">
        <div class="arch-icon-wrap">
          <Icon name="lock" size={24} class="arch-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
        </div>
        <h3>Zero-Trust Downstream Token Vault</h3>
        <p>
          Never expose raw OAuth2 refresh tokens, client secrets, or API keys inside the LLM prompt
          context. With <code>DownstreamTokenBroker</code> and <code>EncryptedKvTokenVault</code>:
        </p>
        <ul class="arch-list">
          <li>Tokens are encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM via <code>authkestra-crypto-util</code>.</li>
          <li>Tool handlers receive an isolated <code>ToolContext</code> scoped to the verified caller.</li>
          <li>Downstream API requests resolve short-lived bearer tokens just-in-time on the server.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="arch-card">
        <div class="arch-icon-wrap">
          <Icon name="square-function" size={24} class="arch-icon" aria-hidden="true" />
        </div>
        <h3>AI-Proof Typestate Builder</h3>
        <p>
          When AI coding assistants generate authentication code, they frequently omit session
          stores, skip token validation, or forget CSRF middleware. Authkestra's Rust typestate
          pattern <code>Engine&lt;S, T&gt;</code> encodes security prerequisites into the compiler:
        </p>
        <div class="code-quote">
          <code>let engine = Authkestra::builder() /* Won't compile until complete */</code>
        </div>
        <p>
          Any incomplete configuration causes a clear compile-time error, preventing LLM hallucinations
          from reaching production.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ai-mcp {
    max-width: var(--ak-layout-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--ak-space-24) var(--ak-space-6);
  }

  .inner {
    position: relative;
  }

  .header {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--ak-space-2);
    padding: var(--ak-space-1) var(--ak-space-3);
    border-radius: var(--ak-radius-full);
    background: hsl(var(--card));
    border: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
    font-size: var(--ak-text-xs);
    font-family: var(--ak-font-mono);
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
    margin-bottom: var(--ak-space-4);
  }

  .pill-icon {
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-3xl);
    letter-spacing: var(--ak-tracking-tight);
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
  }

  .lead {
    margin-top: var(--ak-space-4);
    font-size: var(--ak-text-lg);
    line-height: var(--ak-leading-relaxed);
    color: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
  }

  /* Tiers Grid */
  .tiers-grid {
    margin-top: var(--ak-space-12);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--ak-space-6);
  }

  .tier-card {
    background: hsl(var(--card));
    border: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--ak-space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    transition: border-color var(--ak-duration-fast) var(--ak-ease-out);
  }

  .tier-card:hover {
    border-color: hsl(var(--input));
  }

  .tier-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: var(--ak-space-4);
  }

  .tier-num {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-xs);
    font-family: var(--ak-font-mono);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--ak-tracking-wide);
  }

  .tier-badge {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-2xs);
    background: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-800));
    color: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-300));
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--ak-radius-sm);
    font-family: var(--ak-font-mono);
  }

  .tier-title-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--ak-space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--ak-space-3);
  }

  .tier-icon-wrap {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: var(--ak-radius-sm);
    background: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-800));
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .tier-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
  }

  .tier-desc {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-sm);
    color: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
    line-height: var(--ak-leading-normal);
    margin-bottom: var(--ak-space-5);
  }

  .tier-features {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: var(--ak-space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--ak-space-2);
  }

  .tier-features li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--ak-space-2);
    font-size: var(--ak-text-xs);
    color: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-300));
    line-height: var(--ak-leading-snug);
  }

  .feature-check {
    color: hsl(var(--success-foreground));
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  /* Architecture Sub-Grid */
  .architecture-grid {
    margin-top: var(--ak-space-12);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--ak-space-6);
  }

  .arch-card {
    background: hsl(var(--card) / 0.6);
    border: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--ak-space-6);
  }

  .arch-icon-wrap {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: var(--ak-radius-md);
    background: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-800));
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
    margin-bottom: var(--ak-space-4);
  }

  .arch-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
    margin-bottom: var(--ak-space-3);
  }

  .arch-card p {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-sm);
    color: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
    line-height: var(--ak-leading-relaxed);
  }

  .formula-box {
    margin: var(--ak-space-4) 0;
    padding: var(--ak-space-3);
    background: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-900));
    border: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
    border-radius: var(--ak-radius-sm);
    font-family: var(--ak-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--ak-text-xs);
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .code-quote {
    margin: var(--ak-space-4) 0;
    padding: var(--ak-space-3);
    background: hsl(var(--ak-neutral-900));
    border: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
    border-radius: var(--ak-radius-sm);
    font-family: var(--ak-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--ak-text-xs);
    color: hsl(var(--ak-amber-400));
  }

  .arch-list {
    margin-top: var(--ak-space-4);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--ak-space-2);
  }

  .arch-list li {
    font-size: var(--ak-text-xs);
    color: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
    line-height: var(--ak-leading-normal);
    position: relative;
    padding-left: var(--ak-space-3);
  }

  .arch-list li::before {
    content: "•";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: hsl(var(--primary-accent));
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .tiers-grid,
    .architecture-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .ai-mcp {
      padding: var(--ak-space-16) var(--ak-space-4);
    }
  }
</style>
